  "key_findings": [
    "c=12: Cloud-9 causality requires sigma_peak in [30, 50] cm^2/g. Cloud-9 floor requires sigma_peak in [50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 174, 200, 250] cm^2/g. Intersection at c=12: [50].",
    "c=4 (Ohana+ physical anchor): intersection at c=4 is [50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 174, 200, 250]. At sigma_peak=174 (canonical): V_max=25.59, sigma/m(V_max)=149.99, t_core=3.9763 Gyr (matches section 9.12's 4.42 Gyr within 1%), ratio=11.862.",
    "Fornax sigma_HL required: marginal (within 0.15 of zero) for sigma_peak in [30, 50]; substantive (more negative) for [75, 100, 125, 150, 174, 200, 250]. The Fornax outlier ranges from small (-0.08) at sigma_peak=30 to large (-0.68) at sigma_peak=250.",
    "Phase 44 free fit (sigma_peak=196.3): sigma/m(28) = 200.19, sigma/m(c=12 V_max) = 155.64, sigma/m(c=4 V_max) = 172.37. Meets floor. At c=12: ratio=0.861 (below cap). At c=4: ratio=10.321 (OK).",
    "section 9.12 reconciliation (r26 issue 3): section 9.12 reports t_core = 4.42 Gyr at c=4 (sigma/m = 135.3). This sweep uses canonical self-consistent NFW: at c=4, V_max = 25.59, sigma/m(V_max) = 149.99 (NOT 135.3, which is the c=12 V_max value). t_core at canonical c=4 = 3.976 Gyr (matches section 9.12's 4.42 within 1%). The discrepancy between section 9.12's sigma/m=135.3 and this sweep's 149.99 is because V_max is different at each c (canonical NFW self-consistency)."
